Creating a New Topic/Activity in VIEW on Server Side
=====================================================

This is just an tutorial, so you should do handle it as such.
This means when you try it out, you should not commit it when you
are finished unless it is the topic or activity you really want to add.

Take note that when it is stated that you should change/rename
something in a file it always refers to all occurrences. So e.g.
change "A" to "B" in a file with the content "There is A and also A.xml"
will change the content to "There is B and also B.xml".

When you define a new tag pattern, you should make sure that it does not
conflict with other tags. E.g. in Russian we have the tags "Pr" and "Pred",
if you want to target "Pr" then make sure not to target "Pred" as well.

Take note that this is only the server side of a new topic/activity.
The simplest way to check if this side of your topic/activity works
as expected you need to acquaint yourself with the testing module!

In everything that you change or add you should always change or add
tests accordingly. So if you add a new topic you need to test the
topic. This is very important. This way you can make sure that your
topic works as expected and should it no longer work in the future
it will be noticed as soon as you run the test, don't neglect this!

How to create a new Topic/Activity for Russian
-------------------------------------

We're going to make a copy of the Russian adjective topic and modify it to 
target Russian prepositions instead.

1. Create a new topic json file and edit it.

a. Make a copy of 'view/app/src/main/resources/topics/adjectives.json' and
call it 'preps.json'
b. Change "topic": "adjectives" to "topic": "prepositions" (the same name is used later in the add-on)
c. Change "HFSTRusAdjectivePipe" to "HFSTRusPrepPipe",
d. Change "adjective" into "preposition" in the topic and activity descriptions
e. Optionally you can add or remove activities as you wish in this place

2. Create descriptors for the new topic.

a. Make a copy of 'view/app/desc/operators/HFSTRusAdjectivePipe.xml' and
call it 'HFSTRusPrepPipe.xml' (as specified in preps.json earlier)

Change  "HFSTPostProc_RusAdjectives" to  "HFSTPostProc_RusPreps"

Change  "HFSTRusAdjectivePipe" to  "HFSTRusPrepPipe"

b. Make a copy of 'view/app/desc/operators/HFSTPostProc_RusAdjectives.xml and
call it 'HFSTPostProc_RusPreps.xml' (as specified in HFSTRusPrepPipe.xml earlier)

Change  "HFSTRusAdjectiveEnhancer" to  "HFSTRusPrepEnhancer"

Change "HFSTPostProc_RusAdjectives" to "HFSTPostProc_RusPreps"

c. Make a copy of 'view/app/desc/enhancers/HFSTRusAdjectiveEnhancer.xml' and
call it 'HFSTRusPrepEnhancer.xml' (as specified in HFSTPostProc_RusPreps.xml earlier)

Change "HFSTRusAdjectiveEnhancer" to "HFSTRusPrepEnhancer"

4. Create the enhancer java class for the new topic.

a. Make a copy of  'view/app/src/main/java/werti/uima/enhancer/HFSTRusAdjectiveEnhancer.java' and
call it 'HFSTRusPrepEnhancer.java'  (as specified in HFSTRusPrepEnhancer.xml earlier)

b. Change the TOPIC from "adjectives" to "prepositions" (as specified in preps.json earlier)

c. Change the pos pattern to "Pr\\+"

d. Change the filter pattern to "". Why? Because the filter pattern targets subcategories
that could be selected by the user like "Sg" and "Pl" for "Nouns". "Prepositions" don't have any.

e. Change the exclude token pattern to "". Why? Because the exclude token pattern targets
matches that also can have other readings. E.g. "на" can be "Pr" and "Pcle".
If we don't want to target such cases we put "Pcle" into this pattern. Usually
this pattern needs careful consideration. We accept any match of "Pr" regardless of other
possible readings in this case.

f. Expand the distractor generation located in 'view/app/src/main/java/werti/util/RusDistractorGenerator.java'.
For prepositions we need to add a case called "prepositions" (same as TOPIC in b.) in the
createDistractors function. We can simply select a set of prepositions as distractors here.
Distractors are used in the multiple choice activity.

5. Create tests for the new topic.

a. Make a copy of 'view/app/src/test/java/werti/uima/enhancer/HFSTRusAdjectiveEnhancerTest.java' and
call it 'HFSTRusPrepEnhancerTest.java'

b. Change "HFSTRusAdjectiveEnhancer" to "HFSTRusPrepEnhancer"

c. Modify existing tests or add new tests. Make sure that all edge cases are handled, so that any
situation is handled properly.

d. If you use "IntelliJ IDEA", then you can run the tests via right click on the test class
and selecting Run 'HFSTRusPrepEnhancerTest'. You can also test a specific test inside
the test class. You can also make a breakpoint inside your enhancer and run
the debugger using the test class for simple debugging.
